{"gene1":{"symbol":"PAX4","uniprot":"O43316","is_essential":false,"chromosome":{"chromosome":"7","start":"127610292","end":"127618142","strand":"-1"},"description":{"name":"Paired box protein Pax-4","function":"Plays an important role in the differentiation and development of pancreatic islet beta cells. Transcriptional repressor that binds to a common element in the glucagon, insulin and somatostatin promoters. Competes with PAX6 for this same promoter binding site. Isoform 2 appears to be a dominant negative form antagonizing PAX4 transcriptional activity"},"known_drugs":[]},"gene2":{"symbol":"PAX5","uniprot":"Q02548","is_essential":false,"chromosome":{"chromosome":"9","start":"36833269","end":"37034268","strand":"-1"},"description":{"name":"Paired box protein Pax-5","function":"Transcription factor that plays an essential role in commitment of lymphoid progenitors to the B-lymphocyte lineage (PubMed:10811620, PubMed:27181361). Fulfills a dual role by repressing B-lineage inappropriate genes and simultaneously activating B-lineage-specific genes (PubMed:10811620, PubMed:27181361). In turn, regulates cell adhesion and migration, induces V(H)-to-D(H)J(H) recombination, facilitates pre-B-cell receptor signaling and promotes development to the mature B-cell stage (PubMed:32612238). Repression of the cohesin-release factor WAPL causes global changes of the chromosomal architecture in pro-B cells to facilitate the generation of a diverse antibody repertoire (PubMed:32612238)"},"known_drugs":[]},"pair":{"wgd":false,"family_size":51,"closest":false,"same_chr":false,"interact_bioplex":false,"n_shared_ppi":1,"ppi_network":{"shared":[{"id":"4802","symbol":"NFYC","display":"NFYC (4802)"}],"unique_gene1":[{"id":"10204","symbol":"NUTF2","display":"NUTF2 (10204)"},{"id":"10531","symbol":"PITRM1","display":"PITRM1 (10531)"},{"id":"203245","symbol":null,"display":"203245"},{"id":"2318","symbol":"FLNC","display":"FLNC (2318)"},{"id":"26232","symbol":"FBXO2","display":"FBXO2 (26232)